      "content": "Loading full entity graphs just to render paginated tables is one of the most common causes of database query latency in backend services. When your query brings in lazy proxies, full relationships, and a persistence context tracking objects nobody intends to edit, performance degrades quickly while risking intermittent N+1 queries.\n\nDTO projections bypass the persistence context entirely and instruct the database engine to return only the exact columns required by the client. The real challenge emerges when you combine these projections with dynamic filters, join conditions, and pagination.\n\nA constructor expression inside a JPQL query maps rows directly into immutable record types, avoiding proxy allocation while giving you complete control over the generated SQL join structure. Separating the count query cleanly from the data retrieval query prevents Hibernate from running redundant subqueries across large tables.\n\nApplying projection patterns instead of entity fetching remains one of the simplest architectural adjustments to drastically drop database CPU utilization."
